tonight we are learning more about the  pilot of the plane that crashed  yesterday morning in the south part of  the valley that crash happened in the  area of valley view in pebble  the pilot took off from north las vegas  airport headed to san diego but wanted  to make an emergency landing at the  henderson airport  8 news now reporter kate houston has the  very latest on the investigation  this new video captured on a home  security camera shows the plane  descending  taking a nosedive and then crashing the  national transportation safety board is  leading this investigation  i reached out to the agency it says the  primary focus right now is collecting  information  and documenting the aircraft while no  official identification has been  confirmed  friends of the pilot are identifying him  as robert golo  the owner of air charter express the  business's website promotes air  transportation from san diego  los angeles and las vegas i've known him  for  close to 30 years robert arcy told our  sister station in san diego he just saw  golo last week  arcy says it must have been a mechanical  issue because golo took safety seriously  very cautious very conscientious careful  and safe the ntsb says it won't  determine the cause of the crash this  early in the investigation  the agency says it typically takes 12 to  24 months before a final report is  issued  a preliminary report will be available  in 10 to 12 days  kate houston 8 news now thank you and  the passenger in the plane crash has not  been identified yet
 

